{"description":"Expose `internal/obs` as a live notification stream over the protocol (events.subscribe): ordered notifications for step, dispatch, write, approval and metrics, so a consumer can monitor a run in real time instead of tailing logs. Redaction applies to every event.","acceptanceCriteria":"Subscribers receive ordered, monotonic notifications for steps, EKA writes, approvals and metrics. | Redaction masks secret-like values in every event (no leaks in tests). | Ordering and backpressure semantics are deterministic and documented. | Tests assert the exact event sequence for a fake run."}